I'm not very serious about this release, but since I _know_
I won't do anything about it in the next months I might
just let others know if they want to take over hacking
around with xtron.

This xtron was originally written by Helmut Hoenig, who
states in his README:
     This is an X-version of the well  known  light-race  of
the  TRON-film.  I  actually wrote that program to get a bit
more familiar with X and with communication between programs
through  sockets. (That should be an excuse for writing pro-
grams with such a bad structure.) But at least it  runs  and
besides  the  programming-experience I got, we already had a
lot of fun with it.

I'd add that it's multiuser, communicates thru its own UDP
token ring thing and takes over the complete X display for
graphics (You can't do anything else besides...!).
 
And it's only real fun when played in... say 4 people!
In fact also at this university we had lotsa fun till we
got bored with it.  ;)

Hoenig from Kaiserslautern has become unreachable it seems,
at least his email doesn't work, so here I announce where
the 'Oldenburg' version of xtron resides.

The Ol-version supports nastier auto-players, optional
universe wraparound, settable field sizes, better colour
choices  ;-), etc.

You can saug it.. I mean ftp it from

	ftp 134.106.1.9 (ftp.informatik.uni-oldenburg.de)

	as /pub/irc/xTron_o0.1.t.Z

I know the path says irc, but that's life.

WAIT! WARNING:
Don't expect a quality product... xTron goes more in
the area of dirty hacks concerning Xwindows.

Enjoy if you dare. Ftp at your own risk.   :)
